1
00:00:00,110 --> 00:00:00,680
Part two.

2
00:00:01,180 --> 00:00:03,020
Hitler's empire looked unstoppable.

3
00:00:03,585 --> 00:00:06,140
Then, in one frozen city, it began to break.

4
00:00:06,506 --> 00:00:08,140
Stalingrad, 1943.

5
00:00:08,808 --> 00:00:10,820
An entire German army surrenders.

6
00:00:11,275 --> 00:00:13,200
America fights back across the Pacific.

7
00:00:13,731 --> 00:00:15,260
June 6th, 1944.

8
00:00:15,952 --> 00:00:16,340
D-Day.

9
00:00:16,928 --> 00:00:21,620
About 156,000 Allied troops land in Normandy in a single day.

10
00:00:22,082 --> 00:00:24,020
Germany is crushed from both sides.

11
00:00:24,464 --> 00:00:28,460
In May 1945, with Soviet troops in Berlin, it surrenders.

12
00:00:28,845 --> 00:00:31,120
In August, two atomic bombs fall on Japan.

13
00:00:31,683 --> 00:00:33,360
By September, the war is over.

14
00:00:33,858 --> 00:00:36,840
An estimated 70 to 85 million people died.

